# The paths between ring 3 and the kernel (M5), proved before any real
# thread exists. The self-test retypes ten frames and two TCBs from a RAM
# untyped through l4core::invoke, writes a throwaway address space into the
# frames by hand (the kernel's upper half, a code page, a data and stack
# page, and the last page below 2^47), copies a ring-3 code blob in, and
# drops to ring 3 by iretq. Every later entry from ring 3 reaches the
# test's hook through entry::from_user, which checks GS, the kernel's
# RFLAGS, the frame's place and the last exit's path at each one. The
# thread checks registers on its side too and reports a mismatch through
# DebugHalt. Interrupts taken in ring 3 go through irq::handle and back by
# iretq at any step.
cmdline: test=ring3
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: entry: syscall_entry at 0xffffffff8 # its address moves with the image
expect: , IA32_STAR 0x13000800000000, IA32_FMASK 0x257fd5, EFER.SCE on, IA32_SYSENTER_CS 0
expect: fpu: XCR0 0x3 of
expect: supported, XSAVE area 576 bytes of the TCB's 1024
expect: cpu: CR0 0x80010033 CR4 0x340ee8 EFER 0xd01
expect: ring3: from the 64 KiB untyped in root slot
expect: ring3: dropping to ring 3 at 0x400000 by iretq
# The thread's first state: the user selectors, RFLAGS 0x202, the initial
# FP state read with fnstcw and stmxcsr, FS and GS bases through fs:[0] and
# gs:[0]; every other register 0.
expect: ring3:  1 first entry, by iretq to 0x400000: CS 0x23, SS 0x1b, RFLAGS 0x202, FCW 0x37f, MXCSR 0x1f80, FS and GS bases in place
# The thread prints this line itself, one DebugPutChar per byte, each back
# by sysretq.
expect: ring3: hello from ring 3, one DebugPutChar and one sysretq per byte
expect: ring3:  2 68 DebugPutChar calls, each back by sysretq; every register but RCX and R11 reached the kernel
expect: ring3:  3 syscall with DF, NT and AC set: RFLAGS 0x44646 saved, IA32_FMASK cleared them in ring 0; back with DF and AC, without NT
expect: ring3:  4 RCX and R11 written after a syscall: back by iretq with them
expect: ring3:  5
expect: BP breakpoint (vector 3) from ring 3: error 0x0, RIP 0x4
expect: all 15 registers and DF and AC reached the kernel, which ran with them clear
# XMM0, XMM15, ST0, ST1 and MXCSR across a switch to another TCB's
# initial state and back, checked in the XSAVE areas and by the thread.
expect: ring3:  6 XSAVE64 into the thread's area: XMM0 0xfedcba9876543210:0x123456789abcdef, XMM15 swapped, ST0 1.0, ST1 pi, MXCSR 0x3f80, XSTATE_BV 0x3; XRSTOR64 of the other TCB's initial state, and back
expect: ring3:  7 an unmasked x87 divide by zero pending (FCW 0x37b, FSW 0xb8a4) across XSAVE64 and XRSTOR64: nothing raised in ring 0
expect: ring3:  8
expect: MF x87 floating-point error (vector 16) from ring 3: error 0x0
# QEMU's TCG raises no SIMD exception, so step 9's #XM is skipped there.
expect: ring3: 10 MXCSR 0x1d84: divsd by zero set ZE with ZM clear
expect: ring3: 11 an interrupt taken in ring 3 at 0x4
expect: ring3: 12 syscall with TF set: 0
expect: DB at syscall_entry (the CPU checks TF after IA32_FMASK cleared it); back by sysretq with TF set
expect: ring3: 13
expect: DB debug (vector 1) from ring 3: error 0x0
expect: on IST4, handled on the kernel stack; at the return address, before the next instruction ran; TF cleared
expect: ring3: 14 mov fs and mov gs in ring 3 zeroed IA32_FS_BASE and IA32_KERNEL_GS_BASE; written back from the thread's registers
expect: ring3: 15 fs:[0] and gs:[0] read the markers again; to the tail at 0x7ffffffffff9
# A syscall in the last bytes below 2^47 leaves RCX non-canonical: the
# exit goes by iretq to RIP 0, never by sysretq, and the fetch faults.
expect: ring3: 16 syscall at 0x7ffffffffffe returns to 2^47: RCX 0x800000000000, so exit_frame gives RIP 0 and iretq
expect: entry: warning: RIP 0x800000000000 at or above 2^47 exits as 0
expect: ring3: 17
expect: PF page fault (vector 14) from ring 3: error 0x14, CR2 0x0, RIP 0x0: the fetch at RIP 0, after the iretq exit
expect: ring3: 18
expect: PF page fault (vector 14) from ring 3: error 0x6, CR2 0x600008
expect: ring3: 19
expect: PF page fault (vector 14) from ring 3: error 0x7, CR2 0x400000
expect: ring3: 20
expect: UD invalid opcode (vector 6) from ring 3: error 0x0
expect: ring3: 21
expect: GP general protection (vector 13) from ring 3: error 0x402
# UMIP is on under -cpu max: sgdt faults in ring 3 (H11).
expect: ring3: 22
expect: GP general protection (vector 13) from ring 3: error 0x0
expect: sgdt under UMIP
expect: ring3: 23
expect: GP general protection (vector 13) from ring 3: error 0x0
expect: hlt in ring 3
expect: ring3: 24 done:
expect: exits by sysretq and
expect: by iretq,
expect: FPU ownership dropped
expect: TEST PASS
